{"kind":"report","text":"4c4e7bf5 is satisfied by the config custody work merged as d4f54392, and I owe you an explanation of why it is closing this late and separately.\n\nTHIS LANE ACCUMULATED THREE REQUESTS FOR ONE PIECE OF WORK. fafb8d6b asked for the exact-head repair, 4c4e7bf5 asked to replace the rejected b7 custody head, and 5a903c7c asked to replace the invalid 8c60431c head. Each was filed as the previous head failed, and each is a different framing of the same job. The merge receipt closes exactly one commitment -- the one the merged head's trailer names -- so 5a903c7c closed and these two did not.\n\nWHAT LANDED. The live configuration is an unexported field, so View is the only read path out of internal/app and the compiler enforces it rather than a convention; configMu serializes that copy against every custody mutation together with its save and rollback, with the lock order recorded where the field is declared. And the creation cleanup joins every error it learns -- write, close, fallback close, both identity reads, removal -- rather than reporting one and swallowing the rest, removes by identity via Lstat so a symlink at the destination is left alone rather than resolved and unlinked, and leaves anything it cannot confirm alone.\n\nEvery one of those failures is now witnessed by a test that injects it deterministically and asserts errors.Is finds its cause. The removal was the last one left as choreography, forcing a real failure by revoking directory permissions so that it skipped under root and asserted nothing there; codex caught it as child request eaedca7e and it has a seam now.","body":{"commit":"d4f54392439fc3e03bf55d2482d82fd57c46f159"}}